# Dual-platform watch apps

Wrist Rally ships on **three watch platforms**:

| Platform | Path | Stack |
|----------|------|-------|
| Apple Watch | `watch/`, `shared/` | Swift, SwiftUI, WatchConnectivity |
| Garmin | `garmin/` | Monkey C, Connect IQ |
| Wear OS | `android/domain/`, `android/wear/`, `android/phone/` | Kotlin, Jetpack Compose for Wear OS + phone |

The **iPhone app** (`iPhone/`) is an Apple companion only — not a fourth primary target. The **Android phone app** (`android/phone/`) is the Wear OS companion (history / notes / deletion).

## When adding or changing a feature

Before finishing work, answer:

1. **Does this belong in shared domain logic?** (scoring rules, match lifecycle, persistence shape, product behaviour)
   - If yes: update **`shared/`** (Swift), **`garmin/source/`** (Monkey C), and **`android/domain/`** (Kotlin), and extend tests in `tests/Unit/`, `garmin/source/ScoringEngineTests.mc`, and `android/domain/src/test/`.
2. **Is this watch UX?** Implement on all three platforms where APIs allow, or document a deliberate gap.
3. **Is this Apple-only?** (HealthKit, complications, Live Activities, WatchConnectivity) — note the Garmin/Wear equivalent or mark as deferred in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
4. **Is this Garmin-only?** (Connect IQ widgets, FIT recording, BLE via Garmin Connect Mobile) — note the Apple/Wear equivalent or mark as deferred.
5. **Is this Wear-only?** (Health Services, tiles) — note the Apple/Garmin equivalent or mark as deferred.

## Scoring parity (non-negotiable)

Scoring behaviour must stay identical across platforms:

- Swift source of truth: `shared/Scoring/ScoringEngine.swift`, `shared/Models/`
- Garmin port: `garmin/source/ScoringEngine.mc`, `garmin/source/Models.mc`
- Wear OS port: `android/domain/src/main/kotlin/com/wristrally/domain/ScoringEngine.kt`
- Spec reference: `spec/product.md`

When changing scoring rules, update all three engines and add/adjust tests on all sides.

## Platform mapping

| Concern | Apple | Garmin | Wear OS |
|---------|-------|--------|---------|
| Scoring engine | `shared/Scoring/` | `garmin/source/ScoringEngine.mc` | `android/domain/.../ScoringEngine.kt` |
| Match service | `shared/Services/MatchService.swift` | `garmin/source/MatchService.mc` | `android/domain/.../MatchService.kt` |
| Persistence | `shared/Persistence/` | `garmin/source/MatchStore.mc` | `android/domain/.../MatchStore.kt` |
| Watch UI | `watch/WristRallyWatch/` | `garmin/source/*View.mc` | `android/wear/` |
| Phone UI | `iPhone/` | — | `android/phone/` |
| Glance / complication | `watch/WristRallyComplications/` | widget (not yet built) | tiles (not yet built) |
| Phone sync | `shared/Sync/` | Connect IQ Mobile SDK (not yet built) | `android/sync/` (Data Layer) |
| Workout tracking | HealthKit | FIT / ActivityRecording + FitContributor | Health Services |

## If parity isn't feasible now

- Ship on one platform only when blocked by missing APIs or scope.
- Record the gap in `docs/DECISIONS.md` with platform, reason, and follow-up.
- Do not silently diverge product behaviour between platforms.
